It is you.

413
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:15,950
Stop!

414
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:20,500
I apologize for those who had the
nerve to laugh at Heronut's death.

415
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:24,424
Without enough strength,
you'd only die in vain.

416
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:29,180
Don't waste your life.

417
00:25:30,080 --> 00:25:32,360
Don't sacrifice it for this country.

418
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:39,260
Blue Nose, you never gave up, did you?

419
00:25:39,860 --> 00:25:43,919
You still kept fighting, believing
in what this country could become.

420
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:57,780
And now, thanks to you, Trump
Kingdom, it can finally be reborn.

421
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:11,697
what is that strange creature
behind that tree it almost

422
00:26:11,780 --> 00:26:16,340
looks like a reindeer no
you're wrong It's a monster!

423
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,480
No, don't shoot him!

424
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:20,700
It's a Yeti!

425
00:26:21,660 --> 00:26:22,490
No!

426
00:26:22,573 --> 00:26:23,420
Somebody shoot him!

427
00:26:26,940 --> 00:26:27,780
Jerk face!

428
00:26:28,060 --> 00:26:29,648
He's not a Yeti, you idiot!

429
00:26:29,960 --> 00:26:31,078
He's my new friend!

430
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:32,557
That thing's your friend?

431
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,993
You guys scared him so bad, he ran away!

432
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:38,977
I'll bring him back so you
can meet him, you jerks!

433
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:39,890
Hey!

434
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:41,216
Come back, reindeer!

435
00:26:41,360 --> 00:26:42,957
I want to introduce you to my friends!

436
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:45,360
Would you stop running for a second?

437
00:26:45,620 --> 00:26:47,377
But my friends wouldn't meet you!

438
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:48,617
You wouldn't shoot me!

439
00:26:48,700 --> 00:26:51,112
That's just because I don't know you yet!

440
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:52,500
Hey, slow down!

441
00:26:52,740 --> 00:26:53,916
Where are you going?

442
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:56,697
My friends are back that
way, don't you wanna know?

443
00:26:56,780 --> 00:26:59,497
Doctor, this is for the best, isn't it?

444
00:26:59,580 --> 00:27:01,404
They're not so bad, you'll see!

445
00:27:01,540 --> 00:27:03,877
Come back and meet them,
they're my friends!

446
00:27:03,960 --> 00:27:06,607
My friends like yours,
I don't need anything!

447
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:14,007
Are you sure you're
going to be okay, Dalton?

448
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,420
Yes, I'm fine.

449
00:27:15,820 --> 00:27:17,977
Just feeling a little drained, that's all.

450
00:27:18,060 --> 00:27:18,890
Hey!

451
00:27:18,973 --> 00:27:19,803
You over there!

452
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:23,760
Dr. Kureha!

453
00:27:26,900 --> 00:27:28,597
Yeah, it's good to see you too.

454
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:32,151
Now be useful and take the
injured guy to the medical ward.

455
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:35,397
Nami, you really should stay and
have your illness completely treated.

456
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:36,540
Be quiet.

457
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:41,137
If I don't escape from here now, we won't
be able to set sail for two more days.

458
00:27:41,220 --> 00:27:42,717
You know how worried Vivi is.

459
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:44,177
We need to get her to Alabats.

460
00:27:44,260 --> 00:27:47,217
Quit all this grumbling and
get back to the medical ward.

461
00:27:47,300 --> 00:27:48,130
Move it!

462
00:27:48,460 --> 00:27:49,740
Right now!

463
00:28:06,800 --> 00:28:11,560
Just as I expected, his injuries have
gotten worse due to overexertion.

464
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:17,620
Much better.

465
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:22,440
Dalton, surely you would know
where the key to the arsenal is.

466
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:23,600
Isn't that right?

467
00:28:24,600 --> 00:28:25,500
The arsenal?

468
00:28:25,740 --> 00:28:27,622
Why do you need to get in there?

469
00:28:27,800 --> 00:28:30,457
That's really none of
your business, now, is it?

470
00:28:30,540 --> 00:28:33,737
Wapol always carried that key with
him to keep it secure, he said.

471
00:28:33,820 --> 00:28:37,317
In which case, the key was likely
blown into the sky with him.

472
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,230
Oh, really?

473
00:28:38,313 --> 00:28:39,143
Is that so?

474
00:28:39,226 --> 00:28:40,255
Well, that's a shame.

475
00:28:40,780 --> 00:28:41,610
Dr. Ean.

476
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:42,910
Hmm?

477
00:28:42,993 --> 00:28:45,397
Think we can talk about your
fee for treating our crew?

478
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:46,517
Could you waive it?

479
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:50,247
Oh, and could you go ahead and
discharge me right now as well?

480
00:28:51,080 --> 00:28:52,057
Is that a joke?

481
00:28:52,140 --> 00:28:54,637
Because you should know better
than that by now, girly.

482
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:55,797
For my medical fee,

483
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:59,477
I will be taking all of the cargo and
money you have on that ship of yours.

484
00:28:59,560 --> 00:29:02,678
And you will stay here and
recover for two more days.

485
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:04,677
Nami, she's right, you know.

486
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:06,417
You need to complete your treatment.

487
00:29:06,500 --> 00:29:07,330
I'm fine.

488
00:29:07,413 --> 00:29:08,997
I don't even feel like
I'm gonna die anymore.

489
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:11,668
That isn't exactly a
very convincing reason.

490
00:29:15,740 --> 00:29:17,180
The key to the arsenal.

491
00:29:17,580 --> 00:29:19,345
This is what you needed, yeah?

492
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:22,697
How did you end up with that key?

493
00:29:22,780 --> 00:29:25,897
If that's truly the real one,
how'd you get a hold of it?

494
00:29:25,980 --> 00:29:26,940
I stole it.

495
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:31,277
You've certainly got some guts trying
to negotiate with me like this.

496
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:35,184
You really are an unbelievably
frustrating little girl, you know.

497
00:29:36,140 --> 00:29:36,970
Okay, then.

498
00:29:37,360 --> 00:29:41,097
You don't have to pay my doctor's fee,
but that's as much as I'll agree to.

499
00:29:41,180 --> 00:29:44,117
As a doctor, I can't allow you
to leave in good conscience.

500
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:45,200
Not for two days.

501
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:46,150
Wait a second.

502
00:29:46,233 --> 00:29:48,257
In that case, I'm afraid
we don't have a deal.

503
00:29:48,340 --> 00:29:49,170
Give it back.

504
00:29:49,420 --> 00:29:50,740
Listen here, girl.

505
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:55,517
I have to leave you alone now
and go take care of a few things.

506
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:59,357
If you look in the back room, you might
find a dresser with one of my coats in it.

507
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:02,257
And it's not exactly like I'm
posting any guards on you.

508
00:30:02,340 --> 00:30:06,417
Also, the young man with the spinal fissure
should be well enough to travel by now.

509
00:30:06,500 --> 00:30:09,735
But, girl, don't you even
think about trying to escape.

510
00:30:09,860 --> 00:30:11,480
You guys, come with me.

511
00:30:11,660 --> 00:30:13,277
I have some heavy lifting for you to do.

512
00:30:13,360 --> 00:30:14,301
Okay, all right.

513
00:30:21,560 --> 00:30:25,597
Did she really just tell us to steal
her coat, get Sanji, and sneak out?

514
00:30:25,680 --> 00:30:26,760
I think so.

515
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:29,160
That's what it sounded like to me.

516
00:30:39,220 --> 00:30:41,480
I sure have been running a long time.

517
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:43,642
Night came before I realized it.

518
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:46,357
I don't hear that rubber guy anymore.

519
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:48,793
Looks like I finally shook him, I guess.

520
00:30:49,700 --> 00:30:51,040
This is for the best.

521
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:53,111
I can't leave this place.

522
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,080
I just can't.

523
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:57,584
Looks like a full moon tonight.

524
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:04,600
I can't believe it.

525
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:06,917
Those guys are still looking for me?

526
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:07,882
Come on, Luffy.

527
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:09,497
Why don't you just give it up?

528
00:31:09,580 --> 00:31:12,637
We've been tracking him forever,
and he still hasn't shown up.

529
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:14,557
He's not interested in becoming a pirate.

530
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:16,297
You're just going to have to accept that.

531
00:31:16,380 --> 00:31:17,556
No, that's not true.

532
00:31:17,720 --> 00:31:20,117
I want the reindeer to
be a pirate with us.

533
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:23,617
Just because you want something
doesn't mean it's going to happen.

534
00:31:23,700 --> 00:31:26,980
It's not that I don't want
to go with them. Reindeer!

535
00:31:27,740 --> 00:31:28,570
Reindeer!

536
00:31:28,653 --> 00:31:31,360
Wherever you are, reindeer, come out!

537
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,200
But I'm not going to go.

538
00:31:33,380 --> 00:31:34,260
I can't go.

539
00:31:34,580 --> 00:31:37,040
I'm nothing like them, the humans.

540
00:31:44,700 --> 00:31:45,800
Reindeer guy!

541
00:31:49,820 --> 00:31:50,650
Tony? Me?

542
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:58,725
Kay, you're gonna come on our
ship and be a pirate with us, kay?

543
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:00,430
I can't.

544
00:32:00,513 --> 00:32:01,877
Sure you can't, reindeer.

545
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:03,237
It's a whole lot of fun.

546
00:32:03,320 --> 00:32:05,202
That's not a very good argument.

547
00:32:06,540 --> 00:32:07,370
I can't.

548
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:12,202
I'm not a human, I'm a reindeer!

549
00:32:12,460 --> 00:32:14,872
I have antlers and hooves, don't you see?

550
00:32:16,040 --> 00:32:17,600
I even have a blue nose!

551
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:24,085
Now that you've heard his story, do you
think you can heal the scar on his heart?

552
00:32:25,460 --> 00:32:28,440
Okay, maybe I do want to be a pirate!

553
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:32,697
But I can't ever be one of you!

554
00:32:32,780 --> 00:32:34,600
I'm not human! I'm a monster!

555
00:32:34,980 --> 00:32:38,177
I can't be your friend and I can't
become a pirate on your ship!

556
00:32:38,260 --> 00:32:39,090
You see?

557
00:32:40,260 --> 00:32:41,877
I'm just here to say...

558
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,740
thank you.

559
00:32:44,620 --> 00:32:47,320
I appreciate you asking
me to join your ship.

560
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:50,680
That was really nice, so thank you.

561
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:56,820
I'm going to stay here for now.

562
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:04,040
But if you wanted to, you could
stop by here again. Shut up!

563
00:33:04,320 --> 00:33:05,320
Let's go!

564
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:08,330
Aaaaaaahhhhhh!

565
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:21,828
Most people don't make friends
by telling someone to shut up.
